The '''Shifting Mires''' was a dangerous region of [[Pasaana]]'s [[Lurch Canyon]]. The area contained fields of unstable ground consisting of a [[Color|black]] sand which would swallow nearly everything that got stuck in it. Beneath the Shifting Mires were vast mazes of tunnels created by a [[vexis]], which were also home to the native [[gouge-beetle]]s.

==History==
[[File:QuicksandPasaana.png|thumb|300px|left|The Resistance team sinks into the Shifting Mires sinkhole.]]
Various people fell victim to the sinking fields, often being swallowed and [[Death|dying]] from the dangerous fauna or a lack of [[Foodstuff|food]] and [[water]].<ref name="TROS VD" /> Sometime after the [[Battle of Endor]], the [[Sith cultist|Sith loyalist]] [[Ochi]] died of unknown causes in the tunnels after falling into the Shifting Mires alongside his speeder and [[Blade of Ochi of Bestoon|dagger]].<ref name="Episode IX">{{Film|IX}}</ref>

In [[35 ABY]],<ref name="Year">According to ''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]'' the events of [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']] take place one year after the [[Hosnian Cataclysm]]. Since ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates that to [[34 ABY]], ''The Rise of Skywalker'' takes place in [[35 ABY]].</ref> a group of [[Resistance]] members consisting of [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]], [[Chewbacca]], [[Finn]], [[Poe Dameron]], [[C-3PO]], and [[BB-8]] got caught in the sinking fields and found themselves in the caverns beneath. They retrieved the dagger and had a run-in with a wounded [[vexis]] snake. Rey [[Force healing|Force healed]] the serpent, and it gave safe passage to the group.<ref name="Episode IX" />

